====================================================================================================
 MarXus master equation
====================================================================================================
 RUN SETTINGS
 ------------
 Deck:               /home/peter/Dropbox/Research_Leuven/MarXus/validation/c2h4_ho2_hindered_rotors/input/c2h4_ho2.inp
 Method:             STEADY STATE, OLZMANN (final steady state; steady-state family)
                     J N = R F without an absorbing barrier (Gonzalez-Garcia, Olzmann, PCCP 12, 12290 (2010), eqs. 7, 8)
                     with the thermal rate coefficients of the lowest eigenpair of the same J (eq. 12)
                     and the thermal fates of the wells (Boltzmann distribution of one well as source)
 Solvers:            linear systems: banded Cholesky factorization of the symmetrized J, relative residual <= 1e-8
                     thermal eigenpair: InverseIteration, sum-rule tolerance 1.5e-2 (warning only)
 Parallel:           4 cores (--ncore); the 30 conditions (T, p) in batches of 4 at a time (rayon)
                     BLAS threads per LAPACK call: 1
 Temperatures (K):   300, 500, 700, 1000, 1500, 2000
 Pressures (torr):   7.500616827041697, 75.00616827041698, 750.0616827041697, 7500.616827041697, 75006.16827041698
 Energy grid:        grains of 42.000 cm-1 on a common absolute scale, sums of 1 cm-1 counting cells
 Collisions:         exponential down, exactly normalized (Robertson (ed.), CCK 43 (2019), eq. 4.16), transitions up to 15 <dE_down>
                     low-energy reservoirs where eq. 4.16 fails (sparse states, Robertson 2019, p. 294): the grains from the
                       failing one down form one thermalized state (reservoir state, MESMER manual, Sec. 14.2.1):
                       T = 300 K: W2 5 grains (210 cm-1, 22.0 k_BT below the lowest threshold)
                       T = 500 K: W2 9 grains (378 cm-1, 12.7 k_BT below the lowest threshold)
                       T = 700 K: W2 15 grains (630 cm-1, 8.5 k_BT below the lowest threshold)
                       T = 1000 K: W2 28 grains (1176 cm-1, 5.2 k_BT below the lowest threshold)
                       T = 1500 K: W2 60 grains (2520 cm-1, 2.2 k_BT below the lowest threshold)
                       T = 2000 K: W2 99 grains (4158 cm-1, 0.5 k_BT below the lowest threshold)
                       warning, T = 1500 K: the low-energy reservoir of well W2 reaches 2520 cm-1 above the well bottom, 2.18 k_BT below its lowest reaction threshold (4788 cm-1). The reservoir state assumes Boltzmann equilibrium among its grains and "is usually appropriate for grains which are more than a few kT below the lowest reaction threshold" (MESMER manual, Sec. 14.2.1); results for this well should be checked, e.g. with a finer energy grain (the reservoir forms where the normalization of the exponential-down kernel fails at sparse states).
                       warning, T = 2000 K: the low-energy reservoir of well W2 reaches 4158 cm-1 above the well bottom, 0.45 k_BT below its lowest reaction threshold (4788 cm-1). The reservoir state assumes Boltzmann equilibrium among its grains and "is usually appropriate for grains which are more than a few kT below the lowest reaction threshold" (MESMER manual, Sec. 14.2.1); results for this well should be checked, e.g. with a finer energy grain (the reservoir forms where the normalization of the exponential-down kernel fails at sparse states).
                     collision frequency: Lennard-Jones (per well, below); collision integral Omega(2,2)*: Neufeld, Janzen, Aziz, J. Chem. Phys. 57, 1100 (1972) (default)
 Tunneling:          exact Eckart transmission (Miller, J. Am. Chem. Soc. 101, 6810 (1979), eq. 8)
 Rotors:             7 one-dimensional internal rotors: quantum levels in the Fourier basis of period 2 pi/sigma, convolved with the other degrees of freedom; reduced moment from a geometry: Kilpatrick-Pitzer I(1,3) (default)
                       W2 rotor 1: B 9.938402 cm-1, symmetry 2, potential -0.000039 .. 0.830790 kcal/mol, ground energy 0.155905 kcal/mol, 997 levels up to 28188.7 kcal/mol above the ground; lowest above the ground (kcal/mol): 0.253020 0.456715 0.703733 0.770266 1.277130 1.281169 2.065549 2.065682 3.084614
                       W2 rotor 2: B 1.942945 cm-1, symmetry 1, potential -0.008042 .. 5.969358 kcal/mol, ground energy 0.236392 kcal/mol, 997 levels up to 1379.7 kcal/mol above the ground; lowest above the ground (kcal/mol): 0.235501 0.479277 0.530558 0.563956 0.821328 0.938949 0.990905 1.106612 1.377224
                       W2 rotor 3: B 19.540222 cm-1, symmetry 1, potential -0.000015 .. 5.357391 kcal/mol, ground energy 0.300510 kcal/mol, 997 levels up to 13857.0 kcal/mol above the ground; lowest above the ground (kcal/mol): 0.406470 0.536281 0.803995 1.040977 1.341724 1.670879 2.023764 2.395398 2.781577
                       B3 rotor 1: B 1.961023 cm-1, symmetry 1, potential -0.000013 .. 3.198327 kcal/mol, ground energy 0.128274 kcal/mol, 997 levels up to 1392.0 kcal/mol above the ground; lowest above the ground (kcal/mol): 0.252184 0.495483 0.729209 0.952476 1.042829 1.164081 1.254993 1.362266 1.452151
                       B3 rotor 2: B 19.683031 cm-1, symmetry 1, potential -0.006654 .. 11.648269 kcal/mol, ground energy 0.601209 kcal/mol, 997 levels up to 13960.9 kcal/mol above the ground; lowest above the ground (kcal/mol): 1.062395 1.141376 2.188022 2.231881 3.222394 3.340566 4.276186 4.419624 5.346287
                       B4 rotor 1: B 1.775474 cm-1, symmetry 1, potential -0.020408 .. 37.141151 kcal/mol, ground energy 0.138660 kcal/mol, 991 levels up to 1261.9 kcal/mol above the ground; lowest above the ground (kcal/mol): 0.320495 0.645613 0.975156 1.308920 1.646705 1.988313 2.333552 2.682234 3.034179
                       B4 rotor 2: B 19.913176 cm-1, symmetry 1, potential -0.037105 .. 4.804606 kcal/mol, ground energy 0.116406 kcal/mol, 997 levels up to 14121.4 kcal/mol above the ground; lowest above the ground (kcal/mol): 0.114033 0.397770 0.684825 1.019505 1.376859 1.752889 2.141148 2.536921 2.936095
 Source:             thermal reactant P1 through B3 (P1 -> W2)
                     F(E) ~ rho(E) k(E) exp(-E/kT) of the entrance channels (Pfeifle, Olzmann, IJCK 46, 231 (2014), eqs. 7, 9)
